#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/loop/index.rst:122
msgid ""
"Replayable scalar ``Bind`` statements created by local aliases are not "
"scheduled pipeline operations and should not consume entries in ``order`` or "
"``stage``. For example, in the body below only the copy and store need "
"annotation entries; ``base`` is replayed automatically at each use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/loop/index.rst:127
msgid ""
"for i in T.Pipelined(n, order=[1, 0], stage=[0, 1]):\n"
"    base: T.int32 = i * block\n"
"    T.copy(A[base], shared)\n"
"    T.copy(shared, B[base])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/loop/index.rst:134
msgid ""
"A replayable ``Bind`` may also read a buffer that is not written by the "
"pipeline body, such as ``idx = Ids[i]``. If a ``Bind`` reads a buffer that "
"is written inside the same pipeline body, it is kept as a scheduled "
"statement because the load has a pipeline dependency and cannot be freely "
"replayed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/loop/index.rst:140
msgid ""
"Older code that included replayable scalar ``Bind`` entries in ``order``/"
"``stage`` is accepted for compatibility, but those entries are ignored by "
"the pipeline passes. New code should annotate only the scheduled statements. "
"Avoid setting ``num_stages`` together with manual ``order``/``stage`` unless "
"you intentionally need an explicit depth override."
msgstr ""

